---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';

const updated = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
}).format(new Date('2026-08-25'));
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy policy for Spørretimen: what information is processed in comments, ratings and forms, why, and what rights you have."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Privacy policy"
    lead="Here we explain in concrete terms what is collected on sporretimen.no, why, and what you can do if you want something changed or removed."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container-narrow prose">
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>In short</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Spørretimen is a hobby project, not a registered company. The data controller
          is Jan Sindre Heltne.
        </li>
        <li>
          The forms for contact, guest suggestions and “be a guest” send the message
          directly from your own email client to {site.email}. We do not store these
          form submissions on the website.
        </li>
        <li>
          Comments and ratings are stored in a database (Supabase) because they are
          displayed publicly on the episode page.
        </li>
        <li>We use no analytics tools, ad networks or tracking cookies.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data controller</h2>
      <p>
        Jan Sindre Heltne is responsible for sporretimen.no and the information
        processed here. Spørretimen is a personal hobby project with no connection to
        Jan Sindre’s employer, and is not currently run as a registered business. If you
        have questions about privacy, you can get in touch at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Privacy – Spørretimen')}`}>
          {site.email}
        </a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Comments</h2>
      <p>
        When you leave a comment on an episode, the name you enter and the comment text
        itself are stored in a database, along with the time. Comments are shown
        publicly beneath the episode under the name you provided — so do not write more
        than you are comfortable with everyone seeing.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is consent: you choose to write and submit the comment yourself.
        If a comment is offensive, harassing or otherwise inappropriate, we remove it.
        If you want a comment with your name deleted, get in touch at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will take care of it.
      </p>

      <h2>Ratings</h2>
      <p>
        When you rate an episode, the rating itself (1–6) is stored together with which
        episode it applies to. To prevent the same person voting several times on the
        same episode, your browser stores a random, anonymous code locally (see
        “Browser storage” below). The code is not linked to a name, email address or IP
        address, and cannot be used to identify you.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact forms</h2>
      <p>
        The forms under Contact, Suggest a guest and Be a guest open a pre-filled email
        in your own email client when you submit. The content goes straight to{' '}
        {site.email} as an ordinary email — it is not stored in any database on
        sporretimen.no. The handling of the email itself follows the same rules as any
        other email to {site.email}.
      </p>

      <h2>Browser storage (localStorage)</h2>
      <p>
        The website uses the browser’s local storage — not traditional cookies — for two
        things:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Theme choice:</strong> whether you have selected a light or dark appearance.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Rating code:</strong> the anonymous code mentioned above, which
          prevents double voting.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Both are necessary for the feature you asked for to work, and are not used for
        tracking, profiling or advertising. The information stays in your own browser
        only and is not shared with third parties. You can delete it at any time by
        clearing the browser’s stored data for sporretimen.no.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use no analytics tools (such as Google Analytics), no advertising cookies and
        no cross-site tracking.
      </p>

      <h2>Embedded content from YouTube and Spotify</h2>
      <p>
        The episode pages may show players from YouTube and Spotify. If you play an
        episode directly on the page, YouTube and Spotify may process information about
        you in line with their own privacy terms — that is outside our control. We use
        YouTube’s privacy-enhanced embed mode (youtube-nocookie.com), which limits this
        processing until you actually play the video.
      </p>

      <h2>Images</h2>
      <p>
        Photographs of guests and the host are either taken or approved by the people
        themselves, or made specifically for Spørretimen. We do not use images we do not
        have the right to publish.
      </p>

      <h2>Data processor</h2>
      <p>
        Comments and ratings are stored with <strong>Supabase</strong>, our database
        provider. Access is restricted by rules in the database (Row Level Security):
        visitors can read and add comments and ratings, but cannot edit or delete other
        people’s posts. Removal and moderation are handled by Jan Sindre.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under data protection law (GDPR) you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>be told what information is stored about you,</li>
        <li>have incorrect information corrected,</li>
        <li>have information deleted, such as a comment you have written,</li>
        <li>complain to the <a href="https://www.datatilsynet.no/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Norwegian Data Protection Authority</a> if you believe the processing breaches the rules.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For comments and ratings the simplest route is to get in touch directly at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> — tell us which episode it was
        and roughly when the comment was posted, and we will find it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how the website processes information, we update this page and the
        date at the top.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
